 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63caaf01-44b4-5dc6-a569-9e3a3a5c8859" :question/math-academy-id "q-26811" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y={7}^{x}+4?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we plot the graph of $y={7}^{x}:$\n\n![](images/cd/cd8226319b26b3fef6db6e98efc187b1c474c91bc0252e424151791fda373b95.png)\n\nTo sketch the graph of $y={7}^{x}+4,$ we take the graph of $y={7}^{x}$ and shift it $4$ units up. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,5),$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=4.$\n\n![](images/85/85cc1403ab74e2df97669a7c3363d1abddf6d093c358e888a69b655f1ca7450a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362385 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79daf9dd-814d-562b-b3bc-b066bd2dfb90" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Shift Applied to an Exponential Growth Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41a10cf8-fa76-5d2c-bbfa-53fc9fd443d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={7}^{x}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361128} {:answer/id #uuid "a2e2e43d-b922-5fc1-8f77-36bc7f400904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5({7}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361565} {:answer/id #uuid "af0858d3-eaab-52b2-97be-a12e1d91a0e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={7}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361611} {:answer/id #uuid "d69de0a5-dc56-545f-b406-c4a613d3a95d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5({7}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361793} {:answer/id #uuid "e22e67b0-ee2f-534d-84c4-3a12b2bccb58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={7}^{x}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e22e67b0-ee2f-534d-84c4-3a12b2bccb58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={7}^{x}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361848} :answer-field/id #uuid "45e82ee6-d033-5a82-bd35-1a20f7830c09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b018fdf1-c3ab-56d5-97f8-9a97dabdfd94" :question/math-academy-id "q-99774" :question/problem "![](images/d8/d80c45f952e4c8a65349be524849104b1a76e6ee276186646c6c3facd83c8181.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y={7}^{x}+c.$ Determine the value of $c$ and find the equation of the curve." :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote of $y={7}^{x}$ is $y=0.$ The vertical translation $y={7}^{x}+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-5.$ Therefore, $c=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79daf9dd-814d-562b-b3bc-b066bd2dfb90" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Shift Applied to an Exponential Growth Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15df6806-2868-52a1-bb87-ccc3b49c71eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3({12}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360925} {:answer/id #uuid "25ac3197-829d-5e42-82e7-ccbe433ae931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={12}^{x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360999} {:answer/id #uuid "320d2665-a93e-59a0-94f1-05e1cac58508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={12}^{x}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361058} {:answer/id #uuid "ca540824-50d3-5d23-8a1f-a357a7ac4306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math}